Summary: Install placeholder AMD and NVIDIA DLLs in 64-bit prefixes, for D3DMetal and DXMT
Category: graphics
Kind: feature
Feature: d3dmetal
Origin: crossover
  Version: 26.3.0
  CW-Hacks: 22435
  URL: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-26.3.0.tar.gz
  Files: loader/wine.inf.in
  Changes: CX 25.1.1 lacks these lines; CX 26.3.0's three lines added to
    WineHQ 10.0's [FakeDllsWin64] unchanged
  Note: the wine.inf part of CW HACK 22435; the winemac.drv part is
    winemac-export-macdrv-functions, the ntdll part
    ntdll-export-wine-unix-call. Sikarugir 10.0_8 ships it: its
    share/wine/wine.inf has these lines with this comment; it is the only
    difference in share/
Upstream: no
Why: Have wineboot put placeholder atidxx64.dll, nvapi64.dll and nvngx.dll in
 a 64-bit prefix's system32. CX's comment says only "for D3DMetal". No
 builtin DLLs have those names, so setupapi writes generic placeholder DLLs.
 Outside prefix setup, Wine loads a builtin DLL only if a file of that name
 is in the prefix (find_builtin_without_file in dlls/ntdll/loader.c); with a
 placeholder in system32, a DLL of that name on a renderer's DLL path
 (D3DMetal's three; DXMT ships nvapi64.dll and nvngx.dll) can be loaded.
 Without a renderer path supplying them, loading these names fails with error
 126 as before; programs can only see that the files exist.
Programs: none known
Enable: by WINEDLLPATH_D3DMETAL or WINEDLLPATH_DXMT (ntdll-renderer-dll-paths) supplying DLLs of these names; the files are in every 64-bit prefix
Related: ntdll-renderer-dll-paths, kernelbase-nvngx-d3dmetal, winemetal-stub
Status: 10.0: 2026-11-26: header only (the 11.x copy is now separate). In build0

